    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the slate with a high-ceiling core, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (70.43). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 14% platoon boost against Michael McGreevy and a favorable leadoff spot that maximizes his elite speed potential in our scarcity-driven roster build. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in anchor despite a minor park penalty; his elite xwOBA (.464) and prime protection in the #2 hole against Emerson Hancock make him an auto-start. We are also heavily leaning into the platoon advantages of **Lars Nootbaar** (67.20) and **Junior Caminero** (66.30), both of whom capitalize on soft SP_xERA matchups to provide stable production across the middle of our lineup.\n\nEfficiency concerns have forced us to handle the bench with precision. **Chase Meidroth** (48.42) was the final cut, narrowly missing the rotation behind **Caleb Durbin** (48.56). While **Chase Meidroth** possesses strong park factors, the optimizer preferred the stability of **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s role, even against a tough arm in Jared Jones. Meanwhile, **Hector Rodriguez** (54.99) remains in the lineup despite a 40% rain risk; his favorable platoon splits are too valuable to displace unless a late-afternoon weather cancellation occurs. Conversely, we are keeping **Kazuma Okamoto** (40.37) on the roster as a low-floor play, primarily due to the difficulty of his matchup against Cam Schlittler\u2019s elite 2.81 xERA, which significantly suppressed his projection.\n\nWe remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. Should **Gary Sanchez** or **Christian Yelich** be shuffled down in their respective batting orders, their scores\u2014already hovering near our marginal threshold\u2014could crater. **Christian Yelich** specifically carries risk today, as his -13% platoon adjustment against the southpaw Justin Wrobleski makes him the most volatile piece of our offensive puzzle. Management will monitor the official reports to ensure our SB-heavy strategy isn't derailed by adverse pinch-hitting scenarios or late scratch warnings.",
